# Lockfiles that may exist outside pnpm flow.
#
# package-lock.json is NOT one of them any more: it is tracked, and CI runs
# `npm ci` against it to install Playwright for the PDF contrast gate. The
# rule is dead for the tracked file (git ignores nothing it already tracks)
# and would mislead anyone who deleted and recreated it, so it is removed
# rather than left as a contradiction between this file and the workflow.

# Redis RDB snapshot written when running the local stack from the repo root
dump.rdb

# Claude Code worktrees. Two empty gitlinks were committed here by accident
# (4bcb3d2), with no .gitmodules entry, so every CI checkout logged
# `fatal: No url found for submodule path ... in .gitmodules` during cleanup.
.claude/worktrees/

# Raw credentialed captures from tools/dump_market_snapshot.py --raw-out.
# Unlike tmp/market_snapshot_*.json (aggregates), these are whole feed rows:
# agent names, office details, every field the MLS returned. The three
# showing/remarks fields are stripped by the tool; nothing else is.
tmp/*_raw.json

# Generated by scripts/measure_contrast_by_pixel.py:measure(), which writes the
# Playwright driver next to the repo's own node_modules and unlinks it in a
# `finally`. The path is load-bearing, not laziness: `require('playwright')`
# resolves by walking up from the SCRIPT's directory, so a driver in
# tempfile.mkdtemp() cannot find the package. A `finally` does not run when the
# process is killed outright, so an interrupted measurement leaves this behind
# and the next `git status` reports a 79-line artefact as new source.
_measure_contrast_by_pixel.js
